dlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Betting buzz: Big Ten's odds of national champion four-peat getting slim","description":"Losses by UCLA, Indiana and Ohio State make the Big Ten's chances of winning the national championship this season a long shot.","published":"2026-11-22T04:06:20.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/espn/betting/story/_/id/49921234/college-football-betting-buzz-odds-updates-line-moves-spreads","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Emotional Greg Schiano authors 'special' win, Rutgers' first at PSU since 1988","description":"Less than two weeks after Rutgers announced embattled Greg Schiano would return as coach for a 19th season, the Scarlet Knights stunned Penn State 25-24 on Saturday, their first win over the Nittany Lions since 1988, and just their third this year.","published":"2026-11-22T02:56:26.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50557643/rutgers-authors-special-win-1st-penn-state-1988","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5078165/junior-sherrill","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Junior_Sherrill"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Junior Sherrill","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Junior_Sherrill","description":"American football player (born 2005)","touched":"2026-11-14T07:38:07Z","intro":"Junior Sherrill (born June 14, 2005) is an American college football wide receiver for the Vanderbilt Commodores.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Sherrill attended Lipscomb Academy in Nashville, Tennessee. As a senior, he was the Tennessee Mr. Football after recording 94 receptions for 1,362 yards and 24 touchdowns. In the 2022 state championship game, he had 221 all-purpose yards with four touchdowns and was named the games MVP. Sherrill committed to Vanderbilt University to play college football."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"As a freshman at Vanderbilt in 2023, he played in all 12 games and had 20 receptions for 293 yards and three touchdowns. As a sophomore in 2024, he started 12 of 13 games and recorded 29 receptions for 411 yards with three receiving touchdowns and a kick-return touchdown. As a junior in 2025, he started 11 of 13 games and was second on the team with 54 receptions for 784 yards and seven touchdowns. Sherrill returned to Vanderbilt for the 2026 season."}]}}